            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0905" n="894" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg894"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/797: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Satterthwaite</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-17T11:00:00+03:00">July 17, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 17—7:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. My 18, July 13, 1 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d689-f1"/> Iraq Government
                    appears to be taking lead in opposition to Palestine partition scheme and
                    yesterday afternoon <pb facs="0906" n="895" xml:id="pg895"/> permitted large
                    public demonstration, committee of which has telegraphed Legation requesting
                    support of the United States Government. Official and popular resentment against
                    Emir Abdula [<hi rendition="#italic">Abdullah</hi>] reported increasing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Satterthwaite</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
